    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. regarding the interlocking part, do you think it's better to do a brick-layer style pattern or just stick to column stacking if the load is really heavy? also we sometimes have issues with the top layers feeling \"off\" or slightly unaligned even when we think they're centered. any idea why that happens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For very heavy loads, a brick-layer pattern is generally superior as it distributes weight more evenly and resists shear forces better than simple column stacking. When top layers feel unaligned, it is often due to slight inconsistencies in the pallet base dimensions or accumulated shifting during material handling. Auditing your racking leveler settings and perhaps using standardized, uniform pallets can help minimize these misalignment issues.",
      "source": "target",
